joshua_russo: Well, this is disappointing. [pause=0.5]All that effort to hide an invoice? [pause=0.5]Why didn’t they just burn or shred it?
player: It must mean something, then. [pause=0.5]You said the victim had a history of stealing, right? [pause=0.5]Couldn’t this be related?
joshua_russo: I guess, but what does that tell us? [pause=0.5]The victim hired a locksmith once?
player: Well, this is the first time I’ve seen the name [b]Harper Weissman[/b]. [pause=0.5]It does sound familiar, come to think of it. [pause=0.5]That…[pause=0.5]is the victim’s name, right?
joshua_russo: Nah.[pause=0.5] Just an alias, tons of different names loaded in the chamber, just like any con. [pause=0.5]Honestly, not sure why you’d remember that name in particular.[pause=0.5] Maybe you just liked the sound.
player: I guess… [pause=0.5]Actually, is the address correct too?
